v2.0.0 - 2026-11-03
-------------------
  * New field: log_server, the server_name of the Nginx server
    block that served the request
  * Nginx log_client and log_server are used only if the line
    contains exactly one ", client: ADDR, server: NAME" part,
    and isn't cut by Nginx (a client can send a fake one)
  * Fix: Rule error lines fill log_rule_id, log_rule_file and
    log_rule_line
  * Bounds checks on the stack buffers and the data/error pools,
    the truncated fields get an error message
  * Fix possible crash if the operand of an Apache "Warning."
    message contains ". "
  * Align the error positions in the error pool
  * Remove the CR of a CRLF line ending too
  * Ruby binding: return every rule tag, not only the first
  * Build: "./configure && make" without any binding doesn't run
    make endlessly in bindings/
  * Tests: make check
  * ABI change: logdata has a new field, the SONAME is
    libmsclogparser.so.2, rebuild the bindings and applications

v1.0.1 - 2026-08.14
-------------------
  * Fix possible segfault if the "Warning. ..." message is too
    long in apache's error.log

v1.0.0 - 2026-06-17
-------------------
  * The C structure of the structure library has been
    reorganized, most fields are now accessible via indexed arrays.
  * Some code cleanups

v0.3.0 - 2026-01-19
-------------------
  * Align fields to new format of Apache
    * remove 2nd [client] field lookup
    * add lookup for [remote] if [client] does not exist
  * Align fields to ne format of Apache
    * use [host] field for host if exists
  * Modernize Python3 module build
  * Add pkgconfig related files and entries
  * Replace pointer type to static in method
    of error storage
  * Add boundary check in parsing of log tail

v0.2.0 - 2024-06-21
-------------------
  * Get host from 'host' field in case of Nginx log
  * Increment possible length of [ver]; fix field name
  * URI field was truncated, fixed
  * Long lines caused segfault, fixed
  * Change fields name

v0.1.0 - 2023-02-11
-------------------
  * Initial release
